WEBVTT

00:03.130 --> 00:09.600
Over a century ago, beings that
prey on humans suddenly appeared.

00:14.100 --> 00:19.610
Their absolutely overwhelming strength

00:19.810 --> 00:24.070
quickly pushed humanity to
the brink of extinction.

00:28.160 --> 00:34.500
The surviving humans constructed
three walls: Maria, Rose, and Sina,

00:34.700 --> 00:37.790
which brought them a century of peace.

00:38.000 --> 00:39.420
However...

00:40.330 --> 00:48.550
In the year 845, the Colossal Titan
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared

00:48.760 --> 00:53.350
and destroyed one of humanity's
walls-and everyday life with it.

00:55.270 --> 00:58.190
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

00:58.390 --> 01:02.150
lost twenty percent of its population
and one-third of its territory,

01:02.360 --> 01:07.070
and was forced to
retreat behind Wall Rose.

01:09.950 --> 01:17.580
In the year 850, the Colossal
Titan demolished another wall

01:17.790 --> 01:22.000
and allowed the Titans inside once again.

01:22.210 --> 01:23.420
Eren!

01:23.630 --> 01:25.050
Hurry!

01:31.680 --> 01:37.020
The entire populace was
evacuated two hours later.

01:37.220 --> 01:40.390
Not a single person was eaten by a Titan...

01:41.310 --> 01:47.150
...except for the soldiers who fended
them off and died in the line of duty.

01:47.360 --> 01:48.530
Eren.

01:48.740 --> 01:53.160
As long as I have you,
I can do anything.

02:08.300 --> 02:13.140
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

02:13.340 --> 02:18.600
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

02:18.810 --> 02:23.690
Prayers won't solve anything

02:23.900 --> 02:29.030
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

02:29.240 --> 02:34.320
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

02:34.530 --> 02:36.870
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

02:37.080 --> 02:39.750
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

02:39.950 --> 02:45.130
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

02:45.330 --> 02:50.420
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

02:50.630 --> 02:55.640
consumed with surging bloodlust,

02:55.850 --> 03:02.770
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

03:24.976 --> 03:29.981
Small Blade: The Struggle for Trost, Part 3

03:34.930 --> 03:36.970
Please wait, Captain!

03:37.180 --> 03:38.970
Should the Titans attack,

03:39.180 --> 03:42.220
we supply soldiers won't be able
to hold this position on our own!

03:42.430 --> 03:44.940
Please, Sir! You have to stay here!

03:45.140 --> 03:46.810
Step aside.

03:47.020 --> 03:51.860
I must reorganize the
reinforcements now.

03:52.480 --> 03:55.740
Behind the safety of
the inner gate, you mean?

03:55.950 --> 03:58.280
What the hell are you trying to say?

03:58.490 --> 04:00.330
I'll have you know I'm following regulations!

04:00.530 --> 04:03.950
Obeying established
regulations is a soldier's duty!

04:04.160 --> 04:06.120
B-But, Sir!
If we lose this position...!

04:06.330 --> 04:08.210
Enough of your talk!

04:09.670 --> 04:10.920
Open your mouth again

04:11.130 --> 04:15.260
and I'll be forced to punish
you for treason where you stand!

04:28.310 --> 04:31.690
Why isn't anyone going over the wall?

04:31.900 --> 04:34.400
I'm sure they heard the
bell signaling us to withdraw...

04:49.460 --> 04:52.210
It's all over...

04:52.420 --> 04:54.050
We're done for...

05:03.930 --> 05:05.220
There!

05:05.430 --> 05:08.310
What good is that going to do?

05:17.860 --> 05:20.110
C'mon, Jean! What are we gonna do?!

05:20.320 --> 05:22.740
Ain't anything we can do...

05:22.950 --> 05:25.200
They finally gave the order to withdraw,

05:25.410 --> 05:28.160
but we don't have enough
gas to scale the wall...

05:28.370 --> 05:30.870
We're all gonna die now...

05:31.080 --> 05:33.750
All 'cause of those cowards...

05:33.960 --> 05:35.750
You mean the supply soldiers?!

05:35.960 --> 05:39.010
What's happened to them?!
Were they wiped out?!

05:39.220 --> 05:41.840
Apparently they lost the will to fight.

05:42.050 --> 05:44.220
I can understand the feeling,

05:44.430 --> 05:46.310
but abandoning
their duty to supply us

05:46.520 --> 05:49.100
so they can barricade
themselves inside Headquarters?

05:49.310 --> 05:51.560
And sure enough,
Titans have swarmed the place,

05:51.770 --> 05:53.690
meaning we can't even
get gas for ourselves.

05:53.900 --> 05:55.690
In that case, it's sink or swim!

05:55.900 --> 05:58.400
We'll just have to
take out the Titans there!

05:58.610 --> 06:03.530
Hanging around here's no different!
The Titans will just gather here too!

06:03.740 --> 06:07.700
We'll only use up what little gas we
have left if we keep running aimlessly!

06:07.910 --> 06:11.710
Once we lose our mobility,
we're really done for!

06:11.920 --> 06:15.500
You're actually using
your head for once, Conny.

06:15.710 --> 06:19.670
But do you really think we
have the manpower to pull that off?

06:19.880 --> 06:23.010
Most of the veteran members of
the vanguard have been wiped out.

06:23.220 --> 06:24.300
We're just cadets;

06:24.510 --> 06:28.520
who can possibly take charge of
a suicide mission like that?

06:28.720 --> 06:30.640
Even if someone could,

06:30.850 --> 06:33.730
it's not like we'd stand a chance
against the Titans anyway.

06:33.940 --> 06:39.530
And the supply room's probably got
some that are three or four meters high.

06:39.740 --> 06:44.030
There's no way we could
get anything done in there.

06:44.990 --> 06:47.530
It's hopeless?

06:47.740 --> 06:50.250
What a dull life this was.

06:50.450 --> 06:53.790
If I'd known this would happen,
I would've said something sooner.

06:54.000 --> 06:56.170
Come on, guys! Let's do it!

06:56.380 --> 06:57.500
Get up!

06:57.710 --> 07:01.010
If we all work together,
we're sure to succeed!

07:01.220 --> 07:03.260
I'll take the lead!

07:14.140 --> 07:16.270
Armin! Let's go...!

07:23.320 --> 07:24.320
Reiner.

07:24.530 --> 07:25.410
What now?

07:25.610 --> 07:28.910
Not yet. We have to let them gather first.

07:29.120 --> 07:30.740
It's no use...

07:31.330 --> 07:34.250
However you look at it,
we're not getting out of this city.

07:34.460 --> 07:36.750
We're all dead.

07:36.960 --> 07:40.250
I mean, I'm ready
to die and everything...

07:40.460 --> 07:44.630
It's just... what am I dying for?

07:44.840 --> 07:45.630
Mikasa!

07:45.840 --> 07:47.800
Weren't you with the rearguard?!

07:48.010 --> 07:49.430
Annie!

07:50.060 --> 07:51.930
I understand the gist of the situation.

07:52.140 --> 07:55.100
So I'm sorry for letting
my personal matters interfere...

07:55.310 --> 07:57.440
...but have you seen Eren's squad?

07:57.650 --> 08:00.690
I haven't, but some squads did
make it over the wall...

08:00.900 --> 08:03.570
Actually, we did find Armin over there.

08:05.320 --> 08:06.740
Armin!

08:07.700 --> 08:09.240
Mikasa...

08:09.450 --> 08:13.580
No! I can't bring myself to face her!

08:13.790 --> 08:16.710
All I did was survive for
no good reason...

08:16.920 --> 08:19.130
If I'd known this would happen...

08:19.330 --> 08:22.340
...I would rather have
died with him then instead!

08:24.010 --> 08:24.840
Armin.

08:25.050 --> 08:28.680
You're not hurt, are you?
Are you all right?

08:34.560 --> 08:36.190
Where's Eren?

08:38.520 --> 08:39.940
Armin?

08:51.330 --> 08:52.740
We...

08:54.330 --> 08:57.410
The cadets of Squad 34...

08:57.620 --> 08:59.210
Thomas Wagner...

08:59.420 --> 09:01.340
Nack Tierce...

09:01.540 --> 09:03.880
Milieus Zeremski...

09:04.090 --> 09:06.050
Mina Carolina...

09:06.260 --> 09:08.760
Eren Jaeger...

09:08.970 --> 09:10.550
These five members...

09:10.760 --> 09:13.430
...fulfilled their duties...

09:13.640 --> 09:16.270
...and died valiantly
on the field of battle!

09:19.100 --> 09:20.940
You can't be serious...

09:22.270 --> 09:25.440
So Squad 34 is basically gone...

09:25.650 --> 09:29.780
The same thing'll happen to
us if we try to take the Titans on...

09:29.990 --> 09:32.410
I'm sorry, Mikasa...

09:32.620 --> 09:36.040
It should've been me, not Eren...

09:36.250 --> 09:37.700
I...

09:37.910 --> 09:40.250
...wasn't able to do anything...!

09:40.830 --> 09:42.250
I'm sorry...

09:46.300 --> 09:47.710
Armin.

09:50.970 --> 09:52.430
Calm down.

09:52.640 --> 09:56.720
Now isn't the time to be emotional.

09:57.390 --> 09:59.020
Now get up.

10:00.480 --> 10:01.560
Marco.

10:01.770 --> 10:04.310
If we eliminate the Titans
swarming around HQ,

10:04.520 --> 10:08.030
we can replenish our gas
supplies and get over the wall.

10:08.240 --> 10:09.360
Correct?

10:09.570 --> 10:11.610
Well, yeah...

10:11.820 --> 10:14.450
But even with your help,
there's just too many...

10:14.660 --> 10:15.740
I can handle them.

10:15.950 --> 10:17.370
Huh?!

10:17.790 --> 10:20.160
I'm strong.

10:20.370 --> 10:22.920
Stronger than all of you.

10:23.130 --> 10:24.840
I'm very strong.

10:25.040 --> 10:29.920
As such, I am capable of
annihilating the Titans there!

10:30.130 --> 10:32.800
Even if I have to go it alone.

10:33.470 --> 10:36.180
As for all of you,
you're not only unskilled,

10:36.390 --> 10:39.140
you're also cowards and wimps.

10:39.930 --> 10:41.730
You're a real disappointment.

10:41.940 --> 10:44.480
You can just stay here
and twiddle your thumbs.

10:44.690 --> 10:46.150
Twiddle and watch.

10:46.360 --> 10:49.480
Whoa, Mikasa!
What's gotten into you?!

10:49.690 --> 10:52.490
You're seriously gonna take
on all those Titans by yourself?!

10:52.700 --> 10:54.200
There's no way you can beat them!

10:54.410 --> 10:56.990
If I can't, then I'll die.
It's that simple.

10:57.200 --> 10:57.990
But...

10:58.200 --> 10:59.450
If I win, I'll live.

10:59.660 --> 11:02.620
And the only way to win is to fight!

11:03.290 --> 11:04.710
Hey!

11:09.090 --> 11:12.220
Your way with words
is the real disappointment.

11:12.420 --> 11:15.470
You actually considered
that motivational...

11:15.680 --> 11:18.720
I blame you for this, Eren...!

11:18.930 --> 11:23.100
Hey! Since when were we taught
to let our comrades fight alone?!

11:23.310 --> 11:26.770
Or do you guys want
to end up as actual cowards?!

11:26.980 --> 11:29.440
Never thought I'd hear him say that.

11:35.610 --> 11:40.120
Come on, you cowards,
weaklings, and morons!

11:40.330 --> 11:41.450
Those guys...

11:41.660 --> 11:43.040
Damn it...

11:43.250 --> 11:46.080
All right, let's do it!

11:53.760 --> 11:54.840
Hurry!

11:55.050 --> 11:56.680
Follow Mikasa!

11:56.890 --> 11:58.220
Fight as little as possible!

11:58.430 --> 12:01.010
Get to HQ before you run out of gas!

12:02.140 --> 12:04.520
Man, Mikasa's incredible...

12:04.730 --> 12:07.150
How can she move so fast?!

12:07.350 --> 12:10.270
No! She's using up too much gas!

12:10.480 --> 12:12.650
She's going to run out right away!

12:12.860 --> 12:14.110
Regardless of our skill,

12:14.320 --> 12:17.200
once we lose our mobility
we're completely helpless!

12:24.540 --> 12:27.120
She's not her usual,
composed self at all!

12:27.330 --> 12:29.960
She's trying to distract
herself from her anguish!

12:30.170 --> 12:32.750
It's only a matter of time until she...!

12:37.470 --> 12:38.890
Mikasa!

12:39.090 --> 12:39.970
Damn!

12:40.180 --> 12:41.180
Jean!

12:41.390 --> 12:42.890
You take the lead!

12:43.100 --> 12:44.520
I'll help Armin!

12:44.720 --> 12:46.230
- No, I will too!
- Don't be stupid!

12:46.440 --> 12:47.980
There are still Titans everywhere!

12:48.190 --> 12:50.520
Your skills are needed!

13:03.990 --> 13:05.200
Again...

13:05.830 --> 13:07.750
It's this again...

13:09.370 --> 13:11.790
I've lost my family again...

13:17.590 --> 13:22.010
Do I have to revisit this pain...

13:22.220 --> 13:26.270
...and start all over from here again?

13:46.700 --> 13:50.710
It's no use. We can't
even get near Headquarters.

13:50.920 --> 13:53.920
Unless we're prepared to die...

13:59.090 --> 14:01.510
Crap! He's out of gas!

14:03.140 --> 14:04.550
Stay back!

14:05.220 --> 14:07.270
- Tom! I'll save you!
- No!

14:07.470 --> 14:08.890
It's too late!

14:10.560 --> 14:11.980
Stop!

14:22.490 --> 14:24.450
Why couldn't I stop them...?

14:28.580 --> 14:30.830
Why didn't I stop them?

14:31.040 --> 14:34.710
If I'd made them stop,
this wouldn't have happened...

14:40.170 --> 14:42.260
Am I really cut out for this?

14:43.340 --> 14:46.640
Am I really fit to have
a position of responsibility?!

14:52.440 --> 14:54.060
No!

15:07.490 --> 15:10.410
This world is cruel.

15:10.620 --> 15:11.910
And...

15:12.830 --> 15:14.330
...very beautiful.

15:21.050 --> 15:23.800
It's been a nice life.

15:48.700 --> 15:50.120
Huh?

15:53.870 --> 15:55.290
Why?

15:57.960 --> 16:00.340
I was sure I'd given up...

16:06.890 --> 16:10.810
Why... am I standing up?

16:11.560 --> 16:13.770
Why... am I struggling?

16:22.440 --> 16:24.070
What for?

16:25.740 --> 16:27.160
After all...

16:29.240 --> 16:31.830
There's no point
in living anymore...

16:32.040 --> 16:33.830
So what's driving me?

16:39.170 --> 16:40.590
Fight!

16:40.790 --> 16:43.300
Fight! Fight!

16:44.340 --> 16:45.760
Eren...

16:46.510 --> 16:47.930
Fight!

16:48.590 --> 16:50.390
You have to fight!

16:50.600 --> 16:51.600
Fight!

16:52.060 --> 16:53.680
Fight!

16:56.390 --> 16:58.850
I'm sorry, Eren...

16:59.060 --> 17:01.310
I won't give up anymore...

17:03.940 --> 17:06.610
I'll never give up again...

17:07.610 --> 17:10.030
If I die...

17:10.240 --> 17:13.990
...I'll lose my memories of
you too, on top of everything else.

17:14.200 --> 17:15.410
So...

17:15.620 --> 17:17.410
...I'll do whatever it takes to win!

17:17.620 --> 17:19.670
Whatever it takes to live!

17:36.810 --> 17:38.640
What just happened?!

17:59.410 --> 18:00.830
A Titan...

18:01.920 --> 18:03.540
...is killing...

18:05.420 --> 18:07.260
...another Titan...

18:31.110 --> 18:32.530
Please, Mikasa!

18:32.740 --> 18:34.160
Be all right!

18:38.290 --> 18:39.700
Mikasa!

18:50.260 --> 18:52.720
Mikasa! Are you all right?!

18:52.930 --> 18:54.970
- You two okay?!
- Yeah!

18:55.180 --> 18:57.220
We gotta get out of here!

18:59.970 --> 19:02.640
Crap! Two 15-meter ones!

19:02.850 --> 19:05.810
No, that Titan is...

19:08.570 --> 19:10.190
Huh?!

19:53.320 --> 19:55.360
I-It finished it off?!

19:55.570 --> 19:57.870
It was actually aware of
its weak spot?!

19:58.070 --> 19:59.410
We gotta get out of here!

19:59.620 --> 20:00.870
Before it comes this way!

20:01.080 --> 20:04.000
No, it's not reacting to us.

20:04.210 --> 20:06.830
Any other one
would attack us for sure...

20:07.790 --> 20:10.880
It seemed to grasp the concept
of hand-to-hand combat too.

20:11.090 --> 20:12.590
Just what is it...?

20:12.800 --> 20:15.090
All we can do is chalk it
up as an Abnormal!

20:15.300 --> 20:17.800
We barely know
anything about 'em, after all.

20:18.010 --> 20:19.720
Now let's just hurry to HQ!

20:19.930 --> 20:23.220
Wait! Mikasa's completely out of gas!

20:23.430 --> 20:24.140
Huh?!

20:24.350 --> 20:25.270
Whoa, are you serious?!

20:25.480 --> 20:28.230
Now what are we gonna do?!
We need you!

20:28.440 --> 20:30.110
The answer's obvious!

20:30.320 --> 20:32.690
I don't have much left...

20:32.900 --> 20:34.690
...but hurry and
switch yours with mine!

20:34.900 --> 20:35.860
Armin!

20:36.070 --> 20:37.910
This is our only option!

20:38.320 --> 20:40.870
It'll amount to nothing if I keep it.

20:41.080 --> 20:42.490
Just...

20:42.990 --> 20:45.580
Use it carefully this time.

20:45.790 --> 20:48.120
Everyone's lives are riding on it.

20:49.960 --> 20:55.630
I took charge without any sense
of responsibility for their lives...

20:55.840 --> 21:00.600
For a short time, I had
even thrown away my own life...

21:00.800 --> 21:03.970
All for my own personal reasons.

21:05.180 --> 21:07.350
I'm...

21:07.560 --> 21:09.020
There!

21:09.230 --> 21:13.020
Your mobility gear still works,
and I've given you all my blades.

21:13.230 --> 21:17.700
All I ask is that you
leave me with this one...

21:17.900 --> 21:22.780
I'd rather not get
eaten alive, if I can help it.

21:28.160 --> 21:29.870
N-No way...

21:31.170 --> 21:32.590
Armin.

21:35.000 --> 21:37.630
I'm not leaving you here.

21:47.390 --> 21:49.020
Back there...

21:50.810 --> 21:53.730
...I was completely confused.

21:53.940 --> 21:59.320
I'd never heard of a
Titan killing another Titan before.

22:00.660 --> 22:04.200
But I also felt a
faint glimmer of elation.

22:05.410 --> 22:07.500
Because what I saw...

22:10.250 --> 22:13.750
...looked like the manifestation
of humankind's anger.

22:36.480 --> 22:41.400
Your dreams are where your heart is

22:41.610 --> 22:47.660
They're more fragile than life itself

22:47.870 --> 22:52.330
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

22:52.540 --> 22:59.010
Now, rest in peace

22:59.210 --> 23:10.350
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

23:10.560 --> 23:20.610
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

23:20.820 --> 23:26.570
In this beautiful, cruel world

23:26.780 --> 23:31.750
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

23:31.950 --> 23:37.460
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

23:37.670 --> 23:43.130
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

23:43.340 --> 23:46.760
to anything anymore?

23:53.680 --> 23:56.100
A Titan that kills other Titans.

23:56.310 --> 24:02.320
The sight of it leaves the 104th Cadet
Corps Class awestruck and breathless.

24:02.530 --> 24:04.977
What ultimately appears
before them, though, is...

24:04.977 --> 24:06.780
I Can Hear His Heartbeat: The Struggle for Trost, Part 4
What ultimately appears
before them, though, is...

24:06.780 --> 24:06.970
I Can Hear His Heartbeat: The Struggle for Trost, Part 4
